.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt LIFE_CYCLE-MAC 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm life_cycle-mac
.Nd The MAC algorithm life-cycle
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All message authentication codes (MACs) go through a number of stages in
their life-cycle:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It start
This state represents the MAC before it has been allocated.
It is the starting state for any life-cycle transitions.
.It newed
This state represents the MAC after it has been allocated.
.It initialised
This state represents the MAC when it is set up and capable of
processing input.
.It updated
This state represents the MAC when it is set up and capable of
processing additional input or generating output.
.It finaled
This state represents the MAC when it has generated output.
.It freed
This state is entered when the MAC is freed.
It is the terminal state for all life-cycle transitions.
.El
